From: Alexandr Mironov <7062352+alexandr-mironov@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150-xiaomi-vayu: hold pm8150 l17 on (EXPERIMENT)

With the QLINK pins muxed the modem registers and dies ~3 s later, at what
looks like the first TX. Reading the PMICs every 0.5 s around "online"
shows the modem itself raising l3/l6/l10/l11/l15/l16 on PM8150 within
half a second - and leaving l17 (3.0 V, no consumer anywhere) off. Hold
it on and see.
---

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-vayu-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-vayu-common.dtsi
@@ -366,6 +366,9 @@
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <2856000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <3008000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+			/* The only PM8150 LDO the modem does not raise when the radio
+			 * comes up; 3 V is what a PA wants. Experiment, tracker #6. */
+			regulator-always-on;
 		};
 	};
 
